1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,837
All over Ethiopia, when people want
sparkling water, they simply ask for Ambo.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:14,251
But Ambo is not a bottle. It is a town, a
few hours west of Addis Ababa. This is the

3
00:00:14,251 --> 00:00:15,148
road there.

4
00:00:16,275 --> 00:00:20,947
The minibus leaves before sunrise, and the
city falls away behind the eucalyptus

5
00:00:20,947 --> 00:00:21,297
trees.

6
00:00:24,275 --> 00:00:30,546
The land opens up. Farmers are already in
their fields, and the hills fold into more

7
00:00:30,546 --> 00:00:30,994
hills.

8
00:00:32,275 --> 00:00:35,195
Every bend in the road brings the
mountains a little closer.

9
00:00:39,275 --> 00:00:46,454
Then the town appears. Quiet streets,
students walking to class, the smell of

10
00:00:46,454 --> 00:00:48,132
rain on red earth.

11
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:54,329
Under Ambo, the ground is warm. Water
rises from deep below, full of bubbles:

12
00:00:54,329 --> 00:00:56,976
the same water the whole country drinks.

13
00:00:58,233 --> 00:01:04,242
I drink it here, at the source. It tastes
the same, and completely different.

14
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:12,652
So the next time you order an Ambo,
remember: it is not just water. It is a

15
00:01:12,652 --> 00:01:13,166
place.
